X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Outsiders
DTSTART:20261018T190000Z
DTEND:20261018T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20261018T082156Z
UID:998869
DESCRIPTION:<p>The story that defined a generation\, reimagined as a groun
 dbreaking musical<br /><br />The winner of 4 Tony Awards&reg\;\, including
  Best Musical\, and 2 Drama Desk Awards is <em>The Outsiders</em>.<br /><b
 r />Adapted from S.E. Hinton&rsquo\;s seminal novel and Francis Ford Coppo
 la&rsquo\;s iconic film\, this thrilling new Broadway musical features a b
 ook by Adam Rapp with Justin Levine\, music and lyrics by Jamestown Reviva
 l (Jonathan Clay &amp\; Zach Chance) and Justin Levine\, music supervision
 \, orchestration\, and arrangements by Justin Levine\, choreography by Ric
 k Kuperman &amp\; Jeff Kuperman\, and direction by Tony Award&reg\; winner
  Danya Taymor. The <em>New York Post</em> calls it &ldquo\;The Best New Mu
 sical of the Season.&rdquo\;<br /><br />In Tulsa\, Oklahoma\, 1967\, Ponyb
 oy Curtis\, his best friend Johnny Cade and their Greaser family of &lsquo
 \;outsiders&rsquo\; battle with their affluent rivals\, the Socs. <em>The 
 Outsiders</em> navigates the complexities of self-discovery as the Greaser
 s dream about who they want to become in a world that may never accept the
 m. With a dynamic original score\, <em>The Outsiders</em> is a story of fr
 iendship\, family\, belonging&hellip\;and the realization that there is st
 ill &ldquo\;lots of good in the world.&rdquo\;</p>
LOCATION:Bernard B Jacobs Theatre\, 242 West 45 Street\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
